194   7. Reproducibility
195
196   Analysis scripts generate every reported quantity from
197   the committed probe manifest and raw model outputs.
198   This procedure follows the principle that reports of
199   computational evidence should expose their budget
200   and variation (Dodge et al., 2019). The model and
201   cached data are frozen and checksummed, and each
202   raw output retains its stable probe identifier. Run-
203   ning make all regenerates results.json, the LaTeX value
204   macros, and the paper from cached outputs; running
205   make clean-deep && make all repeats deterministic
206   model inference. Repository gates check frozen inputs,
207   citation resolution, number provenance, pipeline fresh-
208   ness, result sanity, prose style, anonymity, and compi-
209   lation.
